How Scenic Locations Drive the Demand for Farmhouse Plots
Introduction
When it comes to real estate investment, location has always been the most critical factor. But in recent years, the demand for farmhouse plots and NA plots has shifted dramatically towards scenic destinations. Buyers no longer want homes in crowded cities — they’re looking for land surrounded by greenery, hills, riversides, or serene landscapes that combine both luxury and peace.

From the Pune–Mumbai corridor to hill stations like Lonavala, Karjat, and Alibaug, the trend of buying farmhouse plots in scenic areas is booming. For many, it’s about a lifestyle upgrade. For others, it’s a smart long-term investment in appreciating land value.

This article explores why scenic locations fuel demand for farmhouse plots, their investment potential, and why NA plots in these regions are becoming a hot choice for investors in India.
